<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{{ site_title | default("SocialSync") }}</title>
    <meta name="description" content="{{ site_description | default("SocialSync makes it extremely easy to post varied content across Facebook, Instagram, and X with manual or AI workflows.") }}">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:wght@500;700&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
      :root {
        --ink: #1b1f2a;
        --muted: #566277;
        --surface: #ffffff;
        --accent: #1f7a6b;
        --accent-dark: #145548;
        --accent-soft: #e5f3ef;
        --border: rgba(27, 31, 42, 0.12);
        --bg-1: #f4f6f2;
        --bg-2: #dae6f2;
        --bg-3: #f7e0c8;
        --shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(17, 24, 39, 0.12);
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: "Space Grotesk", sans-serif;
        color: var(--ink);
        background: radial-gradient(circle at 10% 10%, var(--bg-3), transparent 60%),
          radial-gradient(circle at 85% 15%, var(--bg-2), transparent 55%),
          linear-gradient(145deg, var(--bg-1), #ffffff 60%);
        min-height: 100vh;
      }

      body::before,
      body::after {
        content: "";
        position: fixed;
        z-index: -1;
        width: 320px;
        height: 320px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        filter: blur(36px);
        opacity: 0.35;
      }

      body::before {
        top: 12%;
        left: -140px;
        background: #f4c9a9;
      }

      body::after {
        bottom: -90px;
        right: -120px;
        background: #c2d8f0;
      }

      img {
        max-width: 100%;
        display: block;
      }

      .wrap {
        max-width: 1120px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 48px 24px 72px;
      }

      header {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: flex-start;
        gap: 16px;
        padding-bottom: 28px;
      }

      .logo {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 14px;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .logo-mark {
        width: 46px;
        height: 46px;
        border-radius: 16px;
        background: var(--accent);
        color: #fff;
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        font-weight: 700;
        font-family: "Fraunces", serif;
        box-shadow: 0 16px 26px rgba(31, 122, 107, 0.3);
      }

      .logo-title {
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.02em;
      }

      .logo-sub {
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        color: var(--muted);
      }

      .hero {
        display: grid;
        gap: 18px;
      }

      .eyebrow {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 10px;
        padding: 6px 14px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: var(--accent-soft);
        color: var(--accent-dark);
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        width: fit-content;
      }

      h1 {
        font-family: "Fraunces", serif;
        font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 4vw, 3.8rem);
        line-height: 1.05;
        margin: 0;
      }

      p.lead {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        line-height: 1.7;
        margin: 0;
        max-width: 820px;
      }

      .hero-images {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
        gap: 18px;
        margin-top: 10px;
      }

      figure {
        margin: 0;
      }

      .image-card {
        background: var(--surface);
        border-radius: 20px;
        padding: 12px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        box-shadow: var(--shadow);
        display: grid;
        gap: 10px;
      }

      .image-card img {
        border-radius: 14px;
      }

      .image-card figcaption {
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        color: var(--muted);
      }

      .section {
        margin-top: 64px;
      }

      .section h2 {
        font-family: "Fraunces", serif;
        font-size: clamp(2rem, 3vw, 2.6rem);
        margin-bottom: 12px;
      }

      .section p {
        color: var(--muted);
        line-height: 1.7;
      }

      .cards {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr));
        gap: 18px;
        margin-top: 22px;
      }

      .card {
        background: var(--surface);
        border-radius: 20px;
        padding: 20px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        box-shadow: 0 18px 40px rgba(27, 31, 42, 0.1);
      }

      .card h3 {
        margin: 0 0 8px;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
      }

      .card p {
        margin: 0;
        color: var(--muted);
        line-height: 1.6;
      }

      .split {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(0, 0.9fr);
        gap: 28px;
        align-items: center;
      }

      .gallery {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr));
        gap: 16px;
      }

      .list {
        list-style: none;
        padding: 0;
        margin: 16px 0 0;
        display: grid;
        gap: 10px;
      }

      .list li {
        position: relative;
        padding-left: 20px;
        color: var(--muted);
        line-height: 1.6;
      }

      .list li::before {
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        top: 9px;
        width: 8px;
        height: 8px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: var(--accent);
      }

      .footer {
        margin-top: 72px;
        padding-top: 24px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 12px;
      }

      .reveal {
        opacity: 0;
        transform: translateY(12px);
        animation: fadeUp 700ms ease forwards;
        animation-delay: var(--delay, 0ms);
      }

      @keyframes fadeUp {
        to {
          opacity: 1;
          transform: translateY(0);
        }
      }

      @media (max-width: 900px) {
        .split {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }

        header {
          flex-direction: column;
          align-items: flex-start;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="reveal" style="--delay: 60ms;">
        <div class="logo">
          <div class="logo-mark">{{ logo_letter | default("S") }}</div>
          <div>
            <div class="logo-title">{{ project_name | default("SocialSync") }}</div>
            <div class="logo-sub">{{ project_tagline | default("AI-aware social content orchestration") }}</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section class="hero reveal" style="--delay: 120ms;">
        <div class="eyebrow">{{ hero_label | default("One-page overview") }}</div>
        <h1>{{ hero_title | default("Extremely easy social posting across Facebook, Instagram, and X.") }}</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          {{ hero_subtitle | default("SocialSync makes it extremely easy to post various types of content to Facebook, Instagram, and X. Content can be manually generated by your team or produced by AI platforms like OpenAI and Gemini, with workflows that keep context flowing from step to step.") }}
        </p>
        <div class="hero-images">
          <figure class="image-card">
            <img src="pages/ai_image_to_ai_post_1.png" alt="AI image to AI post pipeline preview.">
            <figcaption>AI image to AI post with context-aware copy.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="image-card">
            <img src="pages/random_image_to_ai_post_1.png" alt="Random image to AI post preview.">
            <figcaption>Randomized image selection with AI-generated posts.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="reveal" style="--delay: 160ms;">
          <h2>Flexible content workflows that keep AI informed</h2>
          <p>
            Workflows are very flexible and pass context to downstream steps, so every AI output reflects the
            chosen images, instructions, and tone.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="cards">
          <article class="card reveal" style="--delay: 200ms;">
            <h3>Manual Images + Posts</h3>
            <p>Bring your own assets and captions when you already have everything prepared.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card reveal" style="--delay: 240ms;">
            <h3>Manual Images + AI Posts</h3>
            <p>Add a user description and let SocialSync select images randomly from a group while AI writes the post.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card reveal" style="--delay: 280ms;">
            <h3>AI Images -> AI Posts</h3>
            <p>
              Generate images from instructions or juxtaposed options (e.g., "the dog wears a hat/tie with an ocean/mountain
              in the background"), then craft the post using the selected image context.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="card reveal" style="--delay: 320ms;">
            <h3>Video is next</h3>
            <p>Video integration is forthcoming using Sora and other AI assets.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section split">
        <div class="reveal" style="--delay: 180ms;">
          <h2>Instruction-ready pipelines</h2>
          <p>
            Instructions flow through each step so OpenAI, Gemini, or any other model understands the intent,
            constraints, and context.
          </p>
          <ul class="list">
            <li>Capture AI image guidance once and reuse it across profiles.</li>
            <li>Pair AI post prompts with the exact image context that was selected.</li>
            <li>Mix manual and AI sources without losing clarity on tone.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="gallery reveal" style="--delay: 240ms;">
          <figure class="image-card">
            <img src="pages/ai_image_instructions_example_1.png" alt="AI image instruction example.">
            <figcaption>AI image instruction example.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="image-card">
            <img src="pages/ai_post_instructions_example_1.png" alt="AI post instruction example.">
            <figcaption>AI post instruction example.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section split">
        <div class="reveal" style="--delay: 200ms;">
          <h2>UI built for content management</h2>
          <p>The UI is intentionally simple so content, credentials, and instructions stay organized.</p>
          <ul class="list">
            <li>Profiles map to social credentials, image stores, and instruction stores.</li>
            <li>Templates construct posting workflows for each Profile, matching the paths above.</li>
            <li>
              Profiles make it easy to mix manual and AI sources while introducing controlled variability for fresh
              posts every run.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="gallery reveal" style="--delay: 260ms;">
          <figure class="image-card">
            <img src="pages/base_ui.png" alt="SocialSync base UI.">
            <figcaption>Core UI layout for profiles and workflows.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="image-card">
            <img src="pages/ai_image_to_ai_post_template_example_1.png" alt="AI image to AI post template example.">
            <figcaption>Template that binds image and post steps.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <footer class="footer reveal" style="--delay: 240ms;">
        <div>{{ footer_left | default("SocialSync keeps social publishing organized, flexible, and fast.") }}</div>
        <div>{{ footer_right | default("Last updated: " ~ build_time) }}</div>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
